{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 100 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795083300777-reviewer-lane-b.gemini-4-argon.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"\n- P1-1 CONFIRMED CLOSED. Bare `bb native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj` → EXIT 0\n  with full record (self-contained `add-classpath \"src/dev\"` guard before the\n  ns form, same seam, no divergent copy); `--target gambit` refusal EXIT 1;\n  `--target gambit --dry-run` EXIT 0; `--target bogus` EXIT 1.\n- P1-2 SUBSTANTIALLY CLOSED. Remaining drivers converted\n  (run.clj, j5_acceptance, j5_calibrate, j0c_stack, j2_lane, workload_w_run,\n  shell_session, bb.edn smoke:jolt/jolt via new jolt_target_run.clj; child\n  scripts print the identity line, silent when JOLT_TARGET unset).\n  require-chez! + preflight! applied consistently; j2 gates only the\n  jolt-spawning modes (jvm/list/report excluded — no jolt child, correct);\n  shell_session REPL-children exception is documented and coherent\n  (byte-compared transcripts). Residual (P3): j0c/j2/workload_w assert only\n  the driver-level preflight, not each measurement child's own line.\n- P3 CONFIRMED CLOSED. Trailing bare `--target` → clean ex-info\n  \"--target needs a value (chez or gambit)\", EXIT 1 (jolt_launch.clj:56-58).\n\n## NEW P1-A — jolt_target_run.clj silently swallows all child output\n\n`print` before `System/exit` does not flush in babashka (verified: `bb -e\n'(print \"x\") (System/exit 0)'` prints nothing; with `(flush)` it prints).\njolt_target_run.clj uses `(print out)` / `(print err)` immediately before\n`(System/exit exit)` in BOTH modes, so every child's stdout/stderr is lost:\n\n- `bb jolt -e '(+ 1 2)'` → prints header + preflight PASS, exit 0, NO \"3\".\n  The general passthrough task's output contract is broken; callers that\n  parse its stdout now get nothing, silently.\n- `bb smoke:jolt` → prints only \"== jolt-target-run chez --script …\",\n  exit 0. The six PASS checks, RECORD lines and \"SUMMARY ok\" are invisible.\n  The author's verification (exit codes only) could not catch this — the\n  gate still works (assert runs on the captured string) and the exit code\n  still propagates, so it is an output-loss regression, not a correctness\n  hole in the gate itself.\n\nFix: `println`/`(flush)` after the prints (or print to an inherited stream).\nAffected: jolt_target_run.clj script mode + passthrough mode.\n\n## NEW P1-B — jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj identity snippet inside the ns form\n\nThe snippet is placed between the ns name and its :require clause:\n`(ns jolt-j0c-stack-child (when-let [t …]) (:require …))`. Babashka rejects\nany non-clause form inside ns — verified in isolation: \"No matching clause:\nwhen-let\", EXIT 1. Every j0c-stack child therefore crashes at load; the\nj0c-stack lane cannot run. The other five child scripts place the snippet\nafter the ns form and are fine. Fix: move the when-let below the ns form.\n\n## Scope discipline (confirmed)\n\n24 files, all within the owned bounds (src/dev/jolt_*, native/jolt-crypto\nprobes + qualify.clj, bb.edn); no src/cljc|clj, mise.toml, jolt-toolchain.edn,\nfork, or other-worktree changes; autobahn now listed in the sweep with an\nout-of-bounds note. Worktree clean.\n\n## Gates re-run this round\n\nbare qualify EXIT 0; --target gambit refusal EXIT 1; dry-run EXIT 0;\n--target bogus EXIT 1; bare --target clean error EXIT 1; smoke:jolt EXIT 0\nbut output-swallowed (P1-A); smoke:jolt-target chez EXIT 0 (correct output —\nits own driver prints via println); smoke:jolt-target gambit EXIT 0;\nsmoke:jolt --target gambit refused EXIT 1; bb jolt -e passthrough EXIT 0\nwith child stdout lost (P1-A); run-child seam verified correct in isolation.\n\n## RECOMMENDATION: ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES — FINDINGS-OPEN\n\n1. (required) Fix output flush in jolt_target_run.clj (both modes); re-run\n   smoke:jolt and confirm the six PASS lines + SUMMARY reappear, and that\n   `bb jolt -e '(+ 1 2)'` prints 3.\n2. (required) Move the identity snippet out of the ns form in\n   jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj; run one j0c-stack child end-to-end.\n3. (optional P3) Per-child identity asserts in j0c/j2/workload_w (currently\n   preflight-only).\n\n# Final confirmation round — commit 5b827231 (r3, 2026-11-19 ~07:15 GMT)\n\nScope: 5 files, all within owned bounds (jolt_target_run.clj, j0c_stack.clj,\nj0c_stack_child.clj, j2_lane.clj, jolt_profile_compare.cljc). Worktree clean.\n\n- P1-A CONFIRMED CLOSED. `emit!` (print + flush, with a *err* arity) relays\n  child stdout AND stderr in BOTH modes (script + passthrough), flush after\n  every driver println. Re-ran my prescribed checks:\n  - bb smoke:jolt → EXIT 0, all 6 PASS lines present, \"jolt-target: chez\",\n    \"SUMMARY ok\".\n  - bb jolt -e '(+ 1 2)' → EXIT 0, header + identity gate + \"3\" printed.\n- P1-B CONFIRMED CLOSED. Snippet moved after the ns form in\n  jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj; the same latent defect was proactively fixed in\n  jolt_profile_compare.cljc. Ran the j0c stack ladder end-to-end: children\n  loaded, per-child identity asserts green, INFO/OK/ERR lines parsed, table\n  written, EXIT 0.\n- Optional P3 DONE. Per-child fail-closed asserts added: j0c_stack.clj\n  child() asserts before parsing any measurement line (throw → lane aborts\n  before trusting anything); j2_lane.clj run-jolt converts a mismatch into a\n  failing step (:exit 99, FAIL line written to the log) preserving the\n  never-throw step contract. workload_w keeps driver preflight only, with a\n  documented rationale (streaming worker output) — acceptable.\n\n## RECOMMENDATION: ACCEPT — CONFIRMED-CLOSED\n\nAll r1/r2 findings verified fixed with re-runs; both r3 P1 regressions fixed\nand re-verified by output-content checks, not just exit codes; no new issues\nfound in the r3 diff.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 180 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795083300777-engineer-lane-b-target-aware-launchers.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"   \"VERDICT target chez identity \\\"jolt-target: chez\\\" child answered 3: ok\".\n4. bb smoke:jolt-target --target gambit — EXIT 0: \"jolt-target: gambit\", 3,\n   VERDICT ok (gsi 4.9.8 via JOLT_GAMBIT from jolt-env.sh). Re-verified green\n   after the commit hook's formatter reformatted the files.\n5. qualify.clj --target gambit --dry-run — EXIT 0: child identity line +\n   \"DRY-RUN gambit launch seam via $JOLT_GAMBIT ...; no qualification\n   claimed\". qualify.clj --target gambit (no dry-run) — EXIT 1 with the\n   Chez-tier refusal (fail-closed). bb qualify:jolt-libcrypto (chez) — EXIT 0\n   against the symlinked wrapper: \"jolt-target: chez\", full record with\n   :target \"chez\", \"equal to the current :qualified entry\".\n6. bb probe:jolt-j5 --target gambit — EXIT 1, the designed refusal.\n   bb probe:jolt-j5 unavailable (chez) — identity gate PASS\n   (\"child reported jolt-target: chez\"), children launch identically; the 5\n   leg FAILs are the pre-existing layout-3-vs-4 wrapper divergence of the\n   symlinked build/native artifact (environmental, not a launcher change;\n   the child command string is byte-identical to master).\n\n# Deliberately not done\n\n- No suite lanes run (mise.toml/bb.edn wide-input rule); no push; no changes\n  outside the owned files; the fork, ~/workspace/jolt*, build/tools/jolt\n  contents and other worktrees untouched. src/cljc|clj untouched.\n- Gambit qualification itself (running the fork's make gates) is not this\n  round; the seam + smoke + dry-run exercise it as far as this machine's\n  artifacts allow.\n- jolt-env.sh content itself unchanged (JOLT_GAMBIT already exported by\n  bootstrap on master; worktree file is gitignored build output).\n\nDONE\n\n# r2 — review fixes (gemini-4-argon ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES; commit c6023670)\n\nP1-1 FIXED — qualify.clj is self-contained: before the ns form it adds\nsrc/dev to bb's classpath itself (babashka.classpath/add-classpath) unless\nthe seam is already loadable, so the bare\n`bb native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj` that native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj\nspawns works unchanged (reproduced by the reviewer at EXIT 1; now EXIT 0\nboth bare and through -cp). probes/run.clj got the same guard (it now\nrequires the seam). The bb probe:jolt-crypto task additionally gained\n*command-line-args* passthrough so --target reaches run.clj. One seam, no\ndivergent copy.\n\nP1-2 FIXED — remaining brief-named sites converted (23 files in commit\nc6023670):\n- bb.edn smoke:jolt and jolt now run through the NEW generic driver\n  src/dev/jolt_target_run.clj: --script mode runs the repo child through the\n  seam and ASSERTS the child's own identity line fail-closed before trusting\n  its exit; passthrough mode (bb jolt, arbitrary args) runs the fail-closed\n  identity preflight child first. --target gambit is refused fail-closed for\n  script mode (a Clojure script cannot run on bare gsi); the Gambit\n  host-scheme smoke is bb smoke:jolt-target.\n- Drivers converted with --target (default :chez, byte-identical invocations)\n  + require-chez! + jolt-launch/preflight! (fail-closed identity gate):\n  native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj (probe:jolt-crypto), src/dev/\n  jolt_j5_acceptance.clj (test:jolt-j5), src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\n  (calibrate:jolt-j5), src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj (probe:test:jolt-j2 modes),\n  src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj, src/dev/jolt_j0c_stack.clj,\n  src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj.\n- Child-side identity (the seam's child-print-snippet: prints\n  \"jolt-target: <t>\" only when JOLT_TARGET is set, so legacy invocations and\n  JVM legs stay byte-identical): src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj, jolt_test_runner.clj,\n  jolt_j2_probe.clj, jolt_workload_w.clj, jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj,\n  jolt_profile_compare.cljc, jolt_ws_probe.clj, and the native/jolt-crypto\n  probe children provenance.clj, ws_crypto.clj, faults.clj, collect.clj,\n  random_faults.clj, identity.clj. j2_lane's run-jolt and workload_w_run's\n  ProcessBuilder now export JOLT_TARGET into their children.\n- jolt_shell_session's REPL children deliberately get NO JOLT_TARGET: the\n  J3 transcript contract compares jolt vs JVM output byte-for-byte; an\n  identity line would corrupt it (documented in-file).\n- tools/jolt-autobahn/launch.sh (bb.edn autobahn:jolt) remains OUT of bounds\n  per the brief's file ownership — now listed in the sweep (reviewer P3).\n\nP3 FIXED — bare trailing --target raises a clean\n\"--target needs a value (chez or gambit)\" ex-info (jolt_launch.clj\nparse-target-arg), verified.\n\nr2 verification (worktree, foreground, explicit timeouts; post-format\nre-runs all green):\n- bb bootstrap:jolt (with JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR=worktree-local pinned\n  clone, as in r1) EXIT 0 — \"jolt b389f1a7... verified\",\n  \"jolt-target: chez (child identity verified)\", smoke => 3. Note: the bare\n  task against build/tools/jolt still fails on the shared clone's detached\n  697b91ee state (pre-existing divergence another lane left; untouched).\n- bb smoke:jolt EXIT 0 (chez, child identity line printed, driver asserted).\n- bb smoke:jolt-target EXIT 0 both targets; bb jolt -e '(+ 1 2)' EXIT 0\n  (passthrough preflight + child).\n- P1-1 repro: bb native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj (bare) --target gambit\n  --dry-run EXIT 0; bb qualify:jolt-libcrypto EXIT 0 (\"equal to the current\n  :qualified entry\", :target \"chez\" in the record); run.clj's section-10\n  qualify leg PASSed inside the full probe:jolt-crypto run.\n- bb probe:jolt-crypto (full, after building a fresh layout-4 wrapper in the\n  worktree: bb build:jolt-native green, incl. clj -M:antlr-gen --target cpp)\n  — identity gate PASS; every gate PASS except ONE environmental FAIL:\n  random fault injection (NullPointerException at the child's own\n  `@cleanse-var` line) — reproduced WITHOUT the identity line by running the\n  pristine HEAD version of the child, so it is the freshly built wrapper vs\n  the pinned seed interaction, not this branch.\n- bb probe:jolt-crypto --target gambit EXIT 1 (refusal), direct run.clj\n  invocation same.\n- bb probe:jolt-j5 --target gambit EXIT 1 (refusal); probe:jolt-j5\n  unavailable leg: identity gate PASS, 3/5 gates PASS with the fresh\n  layout-4 wrapper (up from 0/5 in r1); the two remaining FAILs are the\n  child REPL's exit-code semantics in absent/wrong-library roots\n  (environmental; child command strings byte-identical to master).\n- probe:jolt-j2 manifest gate fails IDENTICALLY on the master main checkout\n  (four UNLISTED test namespaces) — pre-existing, shown by a control run;\n  the lane's identity gate and child export worked (checked before the\n  manifest gate).\n- bb probe:jolt-ws closure EXIT 0 (child identity line present in the\n  sub-child environment).\n- P3: parse-target-arg [\"--target\"] -> clean \"--target needs a value\".\n- All 24 touched files parse-checked clean with clojure.tools.reader;\n  formatter hook ran on commit; key gates re-run green after formatting.\n\nStill deliberately NOT changed: tools/jolt-autobahn/launch.sh (out-of-bounds\nowner file), the udp shell probes (own jolt-binary resolution, no\njolt-env.sh), jolt:run passthrough (raw binary access, unchanged by design),\nand usage-comment-only mentions. jolt_j5_acceptance's REPL children inherit\nthe shell_session transcript reasoning only where they compare bytes; the\ndriver itself is gated and prefighted.\n\nDONE\n\n# r3 — argon confirmation round (commit 5b827231)\n\nP1-A FIXED — jolt_target_run.clj relayed child output with bare print before\nSystem/exit; babashka does not flush buffered stdout on exit, so the child's\noutput was lost (exit-code-only verification missed it). All relayed output\nnow goes through emit! (print + flush), stdout and stderr, both modes, plus\nflush after every driver println. Verified with actual output below.\n\nP1-B FIXED — the identity snippet sat INSIDE the ns form in\njolt_j0c_stack_child.clj (jolt: \"Ill-formed binding list\", every j0c child\nlane broken at load) — and the same latent defect existed in\njolt_profile_compare.cljc, found in an audit of all nine snippet sites.\nBoth moved after the ns form, as the other child scripts have it.\n\nOPTIONAL DONE — per-child fail-closed identity asserts added where the\ndriver already captures child output: jolt_j0c_stack.clj child() asserts\nthe child's line before reading INFO/OK/ERR; jolt_j2_lane.clj run-jolt\nasserts the captured step log and folds a mismatch into a failing step\n(exit 99), honoring the never-throw step contract. workload_w_run streams\nits worker's output incrementally and keeps the driver preflight only\n(documented).\n\nr3 verification (the reviewer's prescribed checks, actual output lines):\n- bb smoke:jolt — six PASS lines + RECORDs + \"SUMMARY ok\", EXIT 0:\n    jolt-target: chez\n    PASS the closure of yang.antlr.export is exactly it, ... (no transit) [...]\n    PASS yang.antlr.packet/code-points \"aé😀\" = [97 233 128512] [...]\n    PASS yang.antlr.packet/utf8-bytes \"aé😀\" = 7 7\n    PASS yang.antlr.export/byte-offsets of [97 233 128128] = [0 1 3 7] [...]\n    PASS defcfn :blocking usleep(200 ms) returns 0 after >= 200 ms {:result 0, :ms 201}\n    PASS defcfn :blocking strlen ... {:result 7}\n    SUMMARY ok\n- bb jolt -e '(+ 1 2)' — prints header, preflight (\"jolt-target: chez\",\n  PASS identity gate) AND the child's answer \"3\", EXIT 0.\n- one j0c child end-to-end (with JOLT_TARGET=chez exported, exactly as the\n  driver launches it): prints \"jolt-target: chez\", INFO {...} stack report,\n  per-depth \"ERR 256 ERR status -7\" / \"ERR 512 ...\", then DONE, EXIT 0 —\n  loads and completes; at :gambit the Clojure script fails to load (expected;\n  the drivers refuse :gambit before ever launching it).\n- bb smoke:jolt-target EXIT 0 chez; bb smoke:jolt-target --target gambit\n  EXIT 0 (\"VERDICT target gambit identity \\\"jolt-target: gambit\\\" child\n  answered 3: ok\").\n- P1-1 repro: bb native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj --target gambit --dry-run\n  EXIT 0 (bare invocation, the run.clj spawn shape).\n- Bonus: bb jolt --target gambit -e '(+ 1 2)' EXIT 0 — the passthrough's\n  real child ran under gsi (\"PASS identity gate: child reported\n  jolt-target: gambit\").\n- Regression sweep after the r3 edits: bb probe:jolt-ws closure EXIT 0;\n  bb test:jolt-runner-self EXIT 0 (runner child prints its identity line\n  under -M:jolt:jolt-test); bb probe:jolt-crypto full run — every gate PASS\n  except the one KNOWN environmental FAIL (random fault injection NPE,\n  reproduced in r2 on the pristine HEAD child without any snippet: fresh\n  layout-4 wrapper vs pinned seed, not this branch).\n- Formatter hook ran on commit; bb jolt -e and bb smoke:jolt re-run green\n  after formatting; worktree clean.\n\nDONE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/design/datom.world.md'","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n---\n\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nEverything is data.\nInterpretation > abstraction.\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\nRestrictions are a feature.\n\n### Foundational Axioms\n\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n\n## Tuples and Datoms\n\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\n\n## Streams\n\n`dao.stream` is an I/O monad and the system's portable I/O ABI. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\nHosts may install arbitrary local functions, including direct I/O; their availability and migration semantics must be explicit.\nPortable behavior cannot assume them; portable side effects appear as stream emissions. Direct-I/O host modules are explicitly local and non-migratable (owner decision, 2026-10-23).\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\nthe stream's own.\n\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate portably with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Portable agent behavior is specified through stream effects; host-local functions may also perform direct I/O.\n\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\n\n### Host Boundaries\n\nA host boundary is the dao.stream abstraction boundary; implementations do not add contracts.\n[datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) owns the doctrine, owner rulings, taxonomy, floor and custody rules.\n\n## Architectural Commitments\n\n- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\n- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\n- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\n- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\n\n## Design Principles\n\nCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\nStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\n\n**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\ncomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\nwithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\n\n- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\n  ordinary streams.\n- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\n  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\n- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\n- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\n  auto-index observer.\n- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\n  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\n\n**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\ncanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\nshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\n`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\nquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\nconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\nretired `:global` tag in\n[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\ncase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\n\nSee [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../agents/malleability.md) for complete design guidance (cohesion, coupling, bounded complexity, evolution, testing strategy).\nSee [`docs/agents/vocabulary.md`](../agents/vocabulary.md) for domain vocabulary reference (biology, economics, physics, philosophy).\n\n## Code Style\n\n- Prefer simple data over rich types.\n- Prefer total functions over partial ones.\n- Prefer declarative pipelines over imperative logic.\n- Avoid cleverness.\n- Name things after what they do to streams.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Do not invent abstractions that hide streams.\n- Do not suggest mainstream frameworks unless explicitly asked.\n- Do not optimize prematurely.\n- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\n- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\n- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\n  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\n  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\n  leaves to review.\n\n### Problem Decomposition\n\nIf a problem appears complex:\n1. Decompose it into streams.\n2. Identify invariants.\n3. Restrict degrees of freedom.\n4. Make causality explicit.\n5. Let structure emerge from constraints.\n\n## Operational & Specialized Guides\n\n- **Advanced Concepts**: See [`docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`](../agents/advanced-concepts.md) for parallel transport, capability tokens, and entanglement.\n- **Build & Test**: See [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../agents/build-n-test.md) for build, lint, and test commands and TDD guidelines.\n- **Engineering Team Roster**: See [`docs/agents/team.md`](../agents/team.md) for engineering team roles and LLM model assignments.\n- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; each orchestrator session has its own append-only log at `orchestrator-logs/<unix-time-stamp>-<brief-orchestrator-descriptive-name>.md` under the repository root.\n- **Website & Content**: See [`docs/agents/format.md`](../agents/format.md) for `.chp` and `.blog` EDN/Hiccup file specifications.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
