{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -l build/tools/jolt-env.sh build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\nsed -n '1,140p' build/tools/jolt-env.sh\nsed -n '80,110p;153,180p' src/dev/jolt_launch.clj\nrg -n 'bootstrap:jolt|smoke:jolt' bb.edn | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  staff   473 Nov 19 18:00 build/tools/jolt-env.sh\n-rwxr-xr-x@ 1 sto  staff  6159 Oct 22 18:00 build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt\n# written by bb bootstrap:jolt from jolt-toolchain.edn; do not edit\nexport JOLT_CHEZ='/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme'\nexport JOLT_GAMBIT='/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/bin/gsi'\nexport JOLT_HOME='/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/lane-b-launchers/build/bootstrap-test/jolt'\nexport JOLT_PATCHES='/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/lane-b-launchers/build/bootstrap-test/jolt-patches.edn'\n\n(defn launch-command\n  \"The sh -c command string that runs `script` (a path relative to the\n   repo root, or nil for stdin/-e style use) under `target`, with \\\"$@\\\"\n   carrying extra arguments. `alias` extends the -M: alias for :chez\n   (e.g. \\\"jolt-test\\\"). The child sees JOLT_TARGET so it can report its\n   own identity.\"\n  [{:keys [target script alias]}]\n  (let [target (resolve-target target)\n        alias (if (seq alias) (str \":\" alias) \"\")\n        script (if script (str \" \" script \" \"))\n        script (or script \" \")]\n    (case target\n      :chez (str \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && export JOLT_TARGET=chez\"\n                 \" && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt\" alias script \"\\\"$@\\\"\")\n      :gambit (str \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && export JOLT_TARGET=gambit\"\n                   \" && exec \\\"$JOLT_GAMBIT\\\"\" script \"\\\"$@\\\"\"))))\n\n\n(defn run-child\n  \"Run `script` with `args` under `target` (default :chez) via\n   launch-command; answers the babashka process result map with :out/:err\n   strings. `dir` selects the working directory (default: repo root).\"\n  [{:keys [target script alias dir] :or {dir \".\"}} & args]\n  (let [cmd (launch-command {:target target :script script :alias alias})\n        r (apply p/shell {:dir dir :out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                 \"sh\" \"-c\" cmd \"jolt\" (map str args))]\n    {:exit (:exit r) :out (str (:out r)) :err (str (:err r))\n     :target (resolve-target target)}))\n\n\n(defn require-chez!\n  \"Fail-closed refusal for lanes whose children are Chez-tier only (the\n   fork's Gambit FFI tier carries no native wrapper / build CLI yet —\n   host/gambit/ffi/README.md): `lane` names the refusing driver in the error.\"\n  [target lane]\n  (when (= :gambit (resolve-target target))\n    (binding [*out* *err*]\n      (println lane \"FAILED: target gambit is not qualified for this lane;\"\n               \"the Gambit FFI tier does not carry it yet\"\n               \"(jolt fork host/gambit/ffi/README.md); refusing to run\"))\n    (System/exit 1)))\n\n\n(defn preflight!\n  \"Fail-closed identity preflight for a driver: run a trivial child through\n   the same launch seam and assert it reports `target` itself, before any\n   real child's pass/fail is trusted. `context` names the driver in errors.\"\n  [target context]\n  (let [t (resolve-target target)\n        r (run-child {:target t} \"-e\" (identity-probe-form t))]\n    (assert-child-target! {:target t\n                           :output (str (:out r) (:err r))\n                           :context context})\n    (println \"PASS identity gate: child reported\" (identity-line t))\n    t))\n16:  bootstrap:jolt\n26:  smoke:jolt\n27:  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt; Lane B: --target chez|gambit, the child reports jolt-target and the driver asserts it fail-closed — the gambit child runs the same smoke form under $JOLT_GAMBIT)\"\n40:  smoke:jolt-target\n41:  {:doc \"Lane B target-aware launcher smoke: run a trivial child under the requested host scheme through the jolt-launch seam (--target chez, the default, or --target gambit via JOLT_GAMBIT) and fail closed unless the child itself reports jolt-target: <target> (needs bb bootstrap:jolt; the gambit leg needs the mise-pinned gsi)\"\n81:  {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n86:  {:doc \"J7 regression probe: native UDP setup failure injection, exception/buffer cleanup, fatal error seam closure, and receive diagnostics (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n91:  {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n105:  {:doc \"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n119:   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n131:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n141:  {:doc \"J2: staged load probe of the J2 load order under -M:jolt:jolt-test, one namespace per process (load-ok / first failing require / first unresolved symbol / first load-time error + the loaded-libs delta asserting dao.stream.transit absent); logs under build/j2-logs/probe (src/dev/jolt_j2_probe.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n222:  {:doc \"Linearity guard for the jolt dao.host.text override: code-points, unit-count, an ascending code-unit walk and utf8-encode on BMP, astral and mixed strings of 64/256/1024 Ki code points; each 4x input under 8x the time, 1024 Ki under 5 s (src/dev/jolt_text_perf.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
