get lane-target\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:805:      (jlt/preflight! lane-target \"test:jolt-j2 identity gate\"))\nsrc/dev/jolt_target_smoke.clj:54:    (launch/assert-child-target! {:target target :output combined\nsrc/dev/jolt_launch.clj:111:(defn assert-child-target!\nsrc/dev/jolt_launch.clj:173:    (assert-child-target! {:target t\nsrc/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj:72:    (jlt/preflight! t \"calibrate:jolt-j5 identity gate\")\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n   **Failure-reproduction rule (owner ruling 2026-11-01): when a test fails anywhere — a\n   gate, the nightly, or a delegate report — reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the\n   failing test, never the whole suite.** JVM: `clojure -M:test -n <ns>` (a single\n   deftest: add `-v <ns>/<var-name>`). Node: `node target/node-tests.js --test=<ns>`\n   (built by `bb build:yin-repl-node` first only if that test needs the Node REPL).\n   Dart: `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only <ns>[/<test-name>]` (owner ruling\n   2026-11-07: the focus rule runs the failing TEST, not the namespace —\n   `NS/test-name` entries become flutter `--plain-name` filters so only the\n   named deftests execute; fall back to bare `<ns>` only when the failing\n   var inside the namespace is not yet known, and narrow as soon as it is).\n   Fix against the failing test alone, re-run it green, then climb back up\n   (G1 for the home subsystem, G2 for dependents).\n   Dart bug-chases may set `DATOM_FAIL_FAST=1` (owner ruling 2026-11-07): the\n   scoped run stops at the first failure so the report arrives in minutes instead\n   of after the full scoped set. Gate runs never set it — the merge bar needs the\n   complete pass/fail picture. All dart runs use `--reporter expanded`, which\n   streams failure names and positions inline so an interrupted run still retains\n   them (the nightly's compact reporter lost 7 failure names to its 30000s wall,\n   2026-11-06).\n   Merge bar for a fix branch (owner ruling 2026-11-07, sharpening the 2026-11-01\n   ruling): when the work is fixing already-failing tests, the previously-failing\n   tests re-run green IS the merge bar — a fix branch merges on that alone; the\n   G1/G2 climb applies to new feature slices, not to fixes. The full suite still\n   gets its end-to-end confirmation from the daily nightly (04:00 VN), which is\n   what catches collateral damage, not a pre-merge suite run.\n   Never reproduce or chase a failure with the full suite or the slow tier — the full\n   suite is not a debugging tool, and running it locally for one failing test is the\n   exact misuse that drove a laptop load average over 100 (2026-11-01). A failure that\n   only reproduces under the full suite's concurrency is diagnosed with the suite's own\n   logs (its per-shard/per-test output), not by re-running the suite repeatedly.\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master (merged in place by the 2026-11-01 owner ruling)**: The landing gate\n   for a change is the **tests that cover the feature being built** — `bb test:changed`\n   (G2) already includes the reverse-require closure of the changed files, and a wide\n   change still routes to the full quick lane. The complete suite is no longer a\n   per-merge gate: it runs twice a day on the remote hosts (see \"Cadence\" below), so a\n   break is caught within hours without charging every merge ~400 minutes of slow tier.\n5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge\n   (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track\n   (owner decision 2026-10-12), and implicitly twice daily by the scheduled run below.\n   G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.\n\n\nThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\nslice L5) is two tests:\n\n- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\n  processes over real loopback UDP. A JVM publisher with a key file\n  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
